course: french
lesson: 37
title: Olympiad: number-word puzzles ★★★
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: Big French numbers are little sums in disguise: quatre-vingt-dix-sept is "four twenties, ten and seven", so 4 × 20 + 10 + 7 = 97.
explain: From 70 to 99 France counts in a funny old way: 70 is soixante-dix (sixty-ten), 80 is quatre-vingts (four twenties) and 90 is quatre-vingt-dix (four twenties and ten); Belgium and Switzerland say septante for 70 and nonante for 90, and some Swiss say huitante for 80.
explain: Olympiad puzzles love these words because they hide traps: the biggest number is not always the longest word, and vingt hides inside every number from 80 to 99.
explain: Picture a French phone number read aloud: "zéro six, quatre-vingt-dix-huit, soixante et onze..." - the French say phone numbers in pairs, so every chunk must turn into exactly two digits.
explain: The winning habit is the same as in maths: break the word at the hyphens, decide which parts multiply and which add, and never guess when you can count.
fact: Quatre-vingt-dix-sept is a hidden sum: quatre × vingt + dix + sept = 4 × 20 + 10 + 7 = 97.
fact: The longest French number name from 1 to 99, counting letters only, is quatre-vingt-quatorze (94), with 19 letters; 97, 98 and 99 have 18.
fact: Nonante (90 in Belgium and Switzerland) has 7 letters; quatre-vingt-dix has 14 letters, not counting hyphens, so it is 7 letters longer.
fact: The numbers from 71 to 79 are soixante et onze, soixante-douze, ... soixante-dix-neuf, so the only one ending in neuf is 79, soixante-dix-neuf.
fact: From 1 to 99, only 21, 31, 41, 51, 61 and 71 contain the word et: 6 numbers; 81 and 91 have no et (quatre-vingt-un, quatre-vingt-onze).
fact: From 1 to 99, 30 number names contain vingt: the ten from 20 to 29 and the twenty from 80 to 99, which all start with quatre-vingt.
fact: French phone numbers are said in pairs of digits: zéro six, quatre-vingt-dix-huit, soixante et onze, quinze, quarante is 06 98 71 15 40.
fact: Soixante-dix plus vingt-cinq is 95, which in France is quatre-vingt-quinze (80 + 15).
fact: Huitante (80 in some parts of Switzerland) has 8 letters; quatre-vingts has 12, so huitante is 4 letters shorter.
fact: Quatre-vingts has an s when no other number follows it (quatre-vingts pommes, quatre-vingts euros), but loses it when one does (quatre-vingt-cinq).
fact: Every olympiad number puzzle gets easier if you write the digits first, then the words.
exercise: Write quatre-vingt-dix-sept in digits. | 97 | 4 20 10 7 | 87 | 77
exercise: Which sum hides inside quatre-vingt-dix-sept? | 4 × 20 + 10 + 7 | 4 + 20 + 10 + 7 | 4 × 20 × 10 + 7 | 40 + 20 + 17
exercise: Which number from 1 to 99 has the longest French name, counting letters only? | 94, quatre-vingt-quatorze | 99, quatre-vingt-dix-neuf | 97, quatre-vingt-dix-sept | 77, soixante-dix-sept
exercise: How many letters are in quatre-vingt-dix, not counting hyphens? | 14 | 16 | 12 | 13
exercise: How many fewer letters does nonante have than quatre-vingt-dix? | 7 | 9 | 6 | 8
exercise: "Il est entre soixante-dix et quatre-vingts. Son nom finit par neuf." Which number is it? | 79 | 89 | 69 | 99
exercise: From 1 to 99 in France, how many number names contain et? | 6 | 8 | 7 | 9
exercise: Which number has no et? | 81, quatre-vingt-un | 71, soixante et onze | 21, vingt et un | 61, soixante et un
exercise: From 1 to 99, how many number names contain vingt? | 30 | 10 | 20 | 11
exercise: Which is the odd one out: vingt et un, trente et un, quatre-vingt-un, soixante et onze? | quatre-vingt-un, the only one without et | soixante et onze, the only one ending in onze | vingt et un, the only one in the twenties | trente et un, the only one with a t
exercise: Decode the phone number: zéro six, quatre-vingt-dix-huit, soixante et onze, quinze, quarante. | 06 98 71 15 40 | 06 88 61 15 40 | 06 98 71 50 14 | 06 4 20 18 71 15 40
exercise: What is soixante-dix plus vingt-cinq, written in French as in France? | quatre-vingt-quinze | soixante-dix-vingt-cinq | quatre-vingt-cinq | quatre-vingt-dix-cinq
exercise: How many letters shorter is huitante than quatre-vingts? | 4 | 3 | 5 | 6
exercise: Which needs an s at the end of vingt? | quatre-vingts pommes (80 apples) | quatre-vingt-cinq pommes (85 apples) | quatre-vingt-dix pommes (90 apples) | quatre-vingt-un pommes (81 apples)
exercise: Write soixante-quinze in digits. | 75 | 65 | 615 | 60
exercise: What is quatre-vingt-onze? | 91 | 81 | 4 20 11 | 71
test: ★★★ Zoe from Leeds goes, "Easy-peasy: quatre-vingt-dix-sept is 4, 20, 10, 7, so 42107." What did she do wrong? | She read the parts as digits, not a sum | She forgot to count the hyphens as zeros | She should have added all four to get 41 | Nothing, 42107 is right
test: ★★★ Ollie from Manchester says, "Longest name? Gotta be 99, our kid, biggest number wins." Count and settle it. | 94 wins with 19 letters; 99 has 18 | 99 wins with 19 letters | They tie at 18 letters each | 80 wins with 20 letters
test: ★★★ Lily from Brussels says, "Nonante's dead short - I bet it's half as long as quatre-vingt-dix." Is she right? | Yes: 7 letters against 14 | No: 7 letters against 16 | No: 8 letters against 14 | Yes: 6 letters against 12
test: ★★★ Max from Glasgow's mystery number is "between soixante-dix and quatre-vingts, ending in neuf". His pal says, "Aye, it's 89, cos quatre-vingt is in the clue." Who's right? | Neither: it's 79, soixante-dix-neuf | His pal: 89 is right | Max, if he says 99 | Both, 79 and 89 both fit
test: ★★★ Ava from Cork guesses that "loads" of numbers from 1 to 99 contain et, and counts 81 and 91 too. What's the exact count? | 6, because 81 and 91 have no et | 8, with 81 and 91 included | 7, with only 81 included | 9, with 11 too
test: ★★★ Jake from Texas goes, "Y'all, vingt is only in 20 to 29, so ten numbers." What did he miss? | 80 to 99, so it's 30 | 30 to 39, so it's 20 | Nothing, it's 10 | 120 to 129, so it's 20
test: ★★★ Noah from Bristol picks soixante et onze as the odd one out "cos it ends in onze, not un". Why is his teacher not happy? | The shared rule is et: 81 breaks it | His answer is right and the teacher is wrong | Vingt et un is the real odd one out | There is no odd one out at all
test: ★★★ Jayden's mate writes the penpal's number as 06 4201018 71 15 40. What's the mistake? | Quatre-vingt-dix-huit is one pair: 98 | Zéro six should be 6 only | Soixante et onze should be 61 | Quarante should be 14
test: ★★★ Mia from Melbourne writes "nonante-cinq" for soixante-dix plus vingt-cinq. Her French teacher says it's right in Belgium. What's the France answer? | quatre-vingt-quinze | quatre-vingt-cinq | soixante-quinze | quatre-vingt-dix-cinq
test: ★★★ Grace from Geneva writes quatre-vingt with no s and counts 11 letters, so she says huitante is 3 shorter. What went wrong? | Alone, quatre-vingts keeps its s: 12 letters, so 4 | Nothing, 3 is right | Huitante has 9 letters, so it's 2 | Quatre-vingts has 14 letters, so 6
test: ★★★ Ethan from Liverpool must fill in: "quatre-vingt_ pommes, quatre-vingt_-cinq pommes, quatre-vingt_ euros". Which get an s? | The first and the third | Only the first | Only the second | All three
test: ★★★ What would happen if you read 06 98 71 15 40 to a French friend digit by digit, "zéro, six, neuf, huit..."? | She'd understand, but the French say it in pairs | She'd hear a totally different number | She'd think it was a date | She'd think you were speaking Belgian
exam: Ascertain the numerical value denoted by the French expression "quatre-vingt-dix-sept". | 97 | 87 | 4,201,007 | 77
exam: Identify the integer between one and ninety-nine inclusive whose French designation, as used in France, contains the greatest number of letters. | 94 | 99 | 97 | 80
exam: Determine the quantity of integers between one and ninety-nine inclusive whose French designation, as used in France, contains the conjunction et. | Six | Eight | Seven | Five
exam: It is given that the sum of soixante-dix and vingt-cinq is required. State the said sum in the French of France. | quatre-vingt-quinze | nonante-cinq | quatre-vingt-cinq | soixante-quinze
